# Dashboard and workflow guidance

Use this rule when editing the upload flow, session state, dashboard panels, or PDF export.

## Architecture

- `src/store/session-store.ts` is the bridge between uploaded files and rendered analysis
- `src/App.tsx` controls the upload-vs-dashboard state and lazy-loads most analysis panels
- `src/components/dashboard/SessionHeader.tsx` owns export and "new IBT" actions
- `src/lib/pdf-export.ts` is part of the user-visible output, not just an internal helper

## Editing guidance

- Prefer adding or refining computed data in `src/lib/analysis-engine.ts` over scattering fresh calculations across panels
- Keep loading, error, and empty-state behavior intact when touching the upload pipeline
- If a panel depends on optional analysis fields, guard for missing data instead of assuming every session has every channel
- If dashboard content changes materially, check whether PDF output should change too

## Review mindset

- Look for unit drift between dashboard labels and exported reports
- Watch for runtime regressions caused by missing telemetry channels
- Preserve the existing lazy-loaded boundaries unless there is a clear product reason to change them
